                <pb facs="0533" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00/4002: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-10-30T23:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 30,
                                1926—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 31—12:48
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>66. My telegram No. 65, October 29, 5 p.m. President Paz has just sent the
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs and the Minister of War to inform me that in view of
                    the unusual conditions existing at Ceiba the carrying out of his orders [cannot
                    be effected?], however I am informed that Minister of War will be sent at once
                    to Ceiba. Repeated to Ceiba.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
